From 91807dbaf26d5e1be22eaedbff00bfa9b56c5b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Nov 2023 11:44:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 193/572] feat(stm32mp2): tune interconnect bandwidth

Configure Interconnect bandwidth with those parameters:
DDR4, LPDDR4
DDR Regulator enabled
BW GPU limiter disabled
BW CPU limiter enabled with 0x50 (6GB)
CFG_MODEL 00
VDEC priority 1

DDR3
DDR Regulator enabled
BW GPU limiter disabled
BW CPU limiter enabled but sticked to default value with 0x20 (2.4GB)
CFG_MODEL 00

The default ICN QOS VDEC priority (4) is above the default GPU
priority (2) preventing good GPU composition performances during
a h264 1080p60 hw video playback on a 1080p60 display.
Reducing ICN QOS VDEC priority from 4 to 1 (below GPU priority)
improves greatly this use case.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git eb06cf0d0a776e3198fdfe00a811b7255acb04d1 feat(stm32mp2): tune interconnect bandwidth]
Change-Id: I3513bbbefbacec7c91f22db95e9a1fab8a059b6a
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_syscfg.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_syscfg.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_syscfg.c
index 0d1d76cdc2..5ff01b0ce5 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_syscfg.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_syscfg.c
@@ -498,4 +498,18 @@ void stm32mp_syscfg_set_icn_qos(void)
  *	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNDCMIPPBWLCR, U(0x00005002));
  *	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNVDEBWLCR, U(0x00003502));
  */
+
+	/* Enable BW regulator */
+	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNE2EBWRCR, U(0x00000051));
+
+	/* Disable GPU BW limiter */
+	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNGPUBWLCR, U(0x00004009));
+
+	/* Reduce ICN QOS VDEC priority from 4 to 1 */
+	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNQPCR2, U(0x2149865A));
+
+#if STM32MP_DDR4_TYPE || STM32MP_LPDDR4_TYPE
+	/* Change value of CPU BW limiter */
+	mmio_write_32(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_ICNCPU1BWLCR, U(0x00005002));
+#endif
 }
